The C-API to R allows callbacks for few things (such as file selection). 
Their purpose is to allow a seamless integration of R with front-ends or 
IDEs (by replacing them by custom functions). The Windows port of the 
rpy2 never had it working, so this is (unfortunately) expected. All of 
the tests checking the callbacks are expected to fail.

Fixing it is a little more involved, but where there is a will there is 
a way; this is possibly a (contributed) patch away. IIRC Evgeny authored 
the latest patches for the C code addressing Windows compatibility.

L.

PS: For Linux heads I am seeing that the Wine PPA for Ubuntu has just 
fixed the packages. I could install R, Python27, and rpy2 in it.

